    "updated_at": "2022-11-24T00:32:51Z",
    "body": "@domfarolino Do you think the current spec test is clear enough?\r\n\r\nI'm asking because searching for `[ignore higher-layer caching](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#ignore-higher-layer-caching)` in the spec, I can't find any definition for it. \r\n\r\nThe closest for a hint is \r\n\r\n> User agents must remove entries in the [list of available images](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#list-of-available-images) as appropriate given higher-layer caching semantics for the resource (e.g. the HTTP `[Cache-Control](https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7234.html#header.cache-control)` response header) when the [ignore higher-layer caching](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#ignore-higher-layer-caching) flag is unset.\r\n\r\nwhere it alludes to HTTP Caching.\r\n\r\nThanks for the quick reply. You may close if you think the spec is clear enough. :)  \r\n\r\n",
