    "updated_at": "2022-11-24T05:54:17Z",
    "body": "> Hmm, I can't say I'm very familiar with the \"ignore higher-layer caching\" flag at all. \r\n\r\nSame here. And the lack of definition in the rest of the spec had to confusion.\r\n\r\nMy main goal is to make sure that reusing  an image already in the cache because previously fetched and hence ignoring the `lazy` flag is the right way to do things.\r\n\r\nIt seems to be the sane way of doing things, but I'm confused by the current prose. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
